# Browser Controller

MCP server: `browser-controller`. Controls the user's REAL Chrome browser - not headless. All sessions, logins, cookies are already active.

## CRITICAL: Tab-targeting model (v2)

This is a **multi-client** server. Other agents may be working in other tabs right now.
**Never assume which tab your actions hit.** You MUST target a tab explicitly.

### The required flow (instead of "snapshot the active tab")

1. `browser_tabs` with `action: "list"` → get a `tabId` for the tab you want to work in
2. Pass that **same `tabId`** to EVERY page-interaction tool (`browser_snapshot`, `browser_click`, `browser_type`, …)
3. Refs from a snapshot are **only valid for the tabId that produced them**. A ref from tab 10 will never resolve on tab 20.
4. If you need exclusive access to a tab (another agent might touch it), `browser_tabs` with `action: "lock", tabId` first; `action: "unlock"` when done.

If `tabId` is missing on a page tool, you'll get: *"tabId is required. Call browser_tabs list first."*

## Rules

- NEVER close tabs you didn't create
- NEVER navigate away from pages the user is working on without asking
- ALWAYS pass `tabId` — the "active tab" the user is looking at is NOT yours to act on
- Prefer `browser_snapshot` over `browser_screenshot` (cheaper, faster, parseable)
- Several steps you already know → one `browser_batch` call (it stops at the first failing step)
- Refs break after navigation/scroll/DOM changes - re-snapshot before using stale refs
- **Refs recover automatically**: if a ref goes stale but the element still exists, the tool finds it via a robust selector + text/role scan (response carries `via: "fallback"`). If the element was scrolled away entirely, the response carries `freshRefs: [...]` — retry with one of those new refs in the same step, no separate snapshot needed.
- **`isNew: true`** on a snapshot ref means the element appeared since the last snapshot. After an action opens an overlay/dropdown, filter to `isNew` refs instead of re-reading the whole tree.
- After `browser_scroll`, expect `refsMayBeStale: true` on feeds that recycle DOM nodes (Facebook/Instagram/Twitter) — re-snapshot before interacting.
- `browser_evaluate` runs over CDP by default: DevTools-console semantics (top-level `await`, last expression returned) and page CSP does not block it; the yellow "being debugged" banner shows while the debugger is attached. `mode: "scripting"` runs it via chrome.scripting instead — no banner, but a strict page CSP can block it.

## Tools

Every page-interaction tool takes `tabId` (number, required). Listed below.

### Tool discovery (progressive mode)

If only `browser_tools` appears in your tool list, the server is running in progressive-disclosure mode (`BROWSER_CONTROLLER_PROGRESSIVE=1`). Discover and activate tools before calling them:

1. `browser_tools { action: "list" }` — all tool names + one-line summaries
2. `browser_tools { action: "search", query: "click" }` — find tools by keyword
3. `browser_tools { action: "details", tool: "browser_click" }` — full schema AND activates the tool (callable directly afterwards, stays active for the session)

A `"Tool X disabled"` error means you must activate it via `browser_tools {action:"details"}` first.

### Navigation, Tabs & Windows
- `browser_navigate` - Go to a URL (or `"back"` / `"forward"`); returns an inline snapshot unless `snapshot: false`. Params: `url`, `tabId` (optional, defaults to active — pass it anyway), `waitUntil`, `snapshot`
- `browser_tabs` - Params: `action` (list|create|close|focus|reload|lock|unlock), `tabId`, `url`, `active` (create: `false` = background), `window`, `bypassCache`, `fullUrls`
- `browser_resize_window` - Resize/maximize the window holding a tab (responsive checks; it resizes the user's window). Params: `tabId`, `width`, `height`, `state`
- `browser_list_browsers` / `browser_select_browser` - Only when several Chrome profiles are connected. Params: `browserId` (select; `"auto"` = default). List tabs again after switching.

### Interaction (all require `tabId`)
- `browser_click` - Real (trusted) click. Params: `tabId`, `ref` OR `selector` OR `x`+`y`, `button`, `clickCount` (1-3), `doubleClick`, `modifiers`, `trusted`
- `browser_click_text` - Click by visible text (works on portals/overlays missing from snapshots). Params: `tabId`, `text`, `index`, `exact`, `trusted`
- `browser_type` - Real key presses; follow with `browser_press_key` Tab to commit. Params: `tabId`, `ref` OR `selector` (neither = focused field), `text`, `clear`, `trusted`
- `browser_press_key` - Keyboard. Params: `tabId`, `key` (`"Enter"`, `"ctrl+a"`, `"ArrowDown ArrowDown Enter"`), `repeat`, `modifiers`, `ref`, `selector`, `trusted`
- `browser_scroll` - Scroll. Params: `tabId`, `direction`, `amount`, `selector`, `toElement`, `position`, `x`+`y` (wheel at a point)
- `browser_hover` - Hover. Params: `tabId`, `ref` OR `selector` OR `x`+`y`, `trusted`
- `browser_select` - Select from `<select>`. Params: `tabId`, `ref` OR `selector`, `value` OR `label` OR `index`
- `browser_fill_form` - Several fields in one call. Params: `tabId`, `fields` (`[{ ref | selector, value, clear }]`), `submit`
- `browser_drag` - Drag and drop. Params: `tabId`, `startRef` / `startSelector` / `startX`+`startY`, `endRef` / `endSelector` / `endX`+`endY`, `steps`
- `browser_upload_file` - Upload with no file dialog. Params: `tabId`, `ref` OR `selector` (default: first file input), `filePath` OR `files`, or `imageBase64` / `fromScreenshot`
- `browser_act` - Validated action on a `browser_observe` snapshot (see below). Params: `tabId`, `snapshotId`, `action`, `ref`, plus `text` / `value` / `key`… per action

### Reading (all require `tabId`)
- `browser_text` - Visible text, the cheapest read. Params: `tabId`, `selector`, `maxLength`, `mode` (`"article"` = main content), `offset`
- `browser_snapshot` - Accessibility tree with refs. Params: `tabId`, `selector`, `ref`, `compact`, `filter`, `depth`, `maxChars`, `source` (`"dom"` default | `"native"` = Chrome's own computed tree via the debugger)
- `browser_find` - Find elements by natural language. Params: `tabId`, `query`, `limit`, `role`
- `browser_screenshot` - Image over CDP; the result maps image pixels to click `x`/`y`. Params: `tabId`, `format`, `quality`, `maxWidth`, `scale`, `region`, `fullPage`
- `browser_observe` - Compact actionable state + `snapshotId` for `browser_act`. Params: `tabId`, `maxElements`

### Chain, Replay & Record
- `browser_batch` - Several tool calls in ONE round-trip; stops at the first failing step. Params: `actions` (`[{ tool, params }]`, max 200), `tabId` (default for the steps), `continueOnError`, `output` (all|last|errors)
- `browser_shortcuts` - Saved flows with `{{variables}}`. Params: `action` (list|show|save|run|delete), `name`, `description`, `actions` (save), `vars` (run), `tabId`, `continueOnError`, `output`
- `browser_gif` - Record the tab as an animated GIF: a frame after every page-changing action, clicks marked with a red ring. Params: `tabId`, `action` (start|frame|stop|status|export|clear), `width`, `maxFrames`, `activate`, `path`, `clear`. `export` writes the file (default `~/Downloads`) and returns its `path` — give that to the user.

### JavaScript & Dialogs (all require `tabId`)
- `browser_evaluate` - Execute JS like the DevTools console (CDP by default, not blocked by CSP). Params: `tabId`, `expression`, `timeout`, `mode` (`"cdp"` | `"scripting"`)
- `browser_run_action` - Action object `{ execute(params) }` or a plain expression, always via CDP. Params: `tabId`, `code`, `actionParams`
- `browser_handle_dialog` - Handle alert/confirm/prompt (works even on a frozen page). Params: `tabId`, `action`, `promptText`

### Waiting (requires `tabId`)
- `browser_wait` - Wait for an element, text, a URL change or a delay. Params: `tabId`, `selector`, `state`, `text`, `urlIncludes`, `timeout`, `delay`

### Debug (per-tab buffers, capped at 200 entries)
- `browser_console` - Console messages for a tab. Params: `tabId`, `pattern`, `level`, `limit`, `clear`
- `browser_network` - Network requests for a tab. Params: `tabId`, `urlPattern`, `filter`, `failed`, `limit`, `clear`
- `browser_intercept` - Block / redirect / add request headers per tab, captures, HAR export. Params: `action` (set-rules|list-rules|clear-rules|list-captures|export-har), `tabId`, `rules`, `filter`, `limit`. Check `enforcement` in the result: `capture-only` = rules are not applied.

## Safe observe → act

`browser_observe { tabId }` → `browser_act { tabId, snapshotId, action: "click", ref }`. The action re-checks the page first; `DOCUMENT_CHANGED`, `STALE_STATE`, `TARGET_OCCLUDED` or `ACTION_NOT_ALLOWED` mean nothing was done — observe again.

## Multi-agent coordination

- Call `browser_tabs { action: "lock", tabId }` to claim a tab. Other agents' calls to that tab will queue (not fail) until you `unlock`.
- Don't hold locks longer than needed.
- The `browser_tabs list` response includes `lockedBy` per tab so you can see who owns what, and `controlledBy` when another agent is driving an unlocked tab right now (or did within 30 s) — pick another tab or lock it first.

## Workflow

1. `browser_tabs { action: "list" }` → pick a `tabId` (or `action: "create", url`)
2. (optional) `browser_tabs { action: "lock", tabId }`
3. `browser_snapshot { tabId }` to see structure and get refs (valid only for this tabId)
4. Interact: `browser_click { tabId, ref }`, `browser_type { tabId, ref, text }`, …
5. For dropdowns: click trigger → `browser_wait { tabId, delay: 400 }` → look at `isNew` refs / `browser_click_text`
6. Re-snapshot after navigation/DOM changes. If a click returns `freshRefs`, retry with a new ref from it directly.
7. `browser_tabs { action: "unlock", tabId }` when finished
